Subject: Gambatte: hold the second byte of a run until the receiver has run into its next frame (v5irh2)
Series-Step: 4/5 (gambatte link v5irh3)
Origin: hanbang (this project); record name hanbang_gb_v5irh2_from_v5irh.diff
요약: 받는 쪽이 첫 바이트를 읽기 전에 같은 장 안에 둘째 바이트가 와 덮어쓰던 것(포켓몬 카드 GB2 "통신 오류")을 다음 장 반 틱까지 붙잡아 고침.

The first byte of a run that arrives while the frontend sleeps between frames is found at the start of this side's
frame, after the game's own frame-start work, whereas on a cable it arrived during the frame before. A game that reads it
once a frame (copied to RAM by its serial interrupt) then reads it only in the next frame, so when the sender waits about
a frame or more before its second byte (gap >= 70224 cycles) the second byte must not arrive before that: Pokemon Trading
Card GB2's START side waits a $1000 loop after the 21 answer, the half-frame allowance used to bring its next byte
inside the same frame, it overwrote the first one and the game never became the client. Such a second byte now also waits
until this side's next frame has run half a 240 Hz tick (Card GB 1 still works: its client gives up if the byte is more
than about a third of a frame later). New counters: frames run, frame of the first byte, time first seen in a frame.

